class.description:
Holds only the [member velocity] state needed to continue a damped-spring simulation from one call to [method update] to the next. [DampedSpring] doesn't store the spring's current value or target itself -- both are passed into [method update] each time, along with a [DampedSpringParameters] resource describing how the spring should respond.
This lets a single [DampedSpring] instance be reused for different values and targets, and lets one [DampedSpringParameters] resource be shared by many springs at once.
See also [DampedSpring2D] and [DampedSpring3D] for the [Vector2]/[Vector3] equivalents.
[codeblock]
var spring := DampedSpring.new()
var spring_params := DampedSpringParameters.new()
var value := 0.0

func _process(delta: float) -> void:
    value = spring.update(delta, value, target_value, spring_params)
[/codeblock]
